lantic wealth became a key component of kings\' strategies to instill political order. Whereas local markets economically integrated town and countryside, it was luxuries acquired in trade that served as the political glue binding rural lords to urban royal dynasties.” '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 840, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 765})
